# Review of claim-to-section ratio

The note makes two linked claims. An operative revision requires an installed
change that later work depends on within a named redesign class. Repeatability
requires the successor to preserve a route for revising that same class again.
The four substantive headings provide space for three distinct jobs.
Operational test makes both claims checkable, Evidence calibrates what the
reported cases establish, and Reasoning handles two harder inferences about
how human participation and replaceable admission rules can preserve a path.
